[0m [1m[38;5;98mPODS[0m - every pod and container of the namespace, live usage against what it asked for.
   [1mHealth line[0m (every view): ready pods, restarts, OOM risk, OOMKilled, pods without a memory
               limit, CPU / memory against limits, degraded / rolling workloads, events of 15 min.
   Grouped by workload (Deployment / StatefulSet / ...): the workload line is the sum of its pods.
   [1mACTUAL[0m      CPU in millicores (1000m = 1 core) and memory in MiB, measured by metrics-server.
               T = trend since the last poll: up / down / flat.
   [1mASSIGNED[0m    requests (reserved for scheduling) and limits (hard cap) from the pod spec.
   [1mUTILISATION[0m used as % of request and of limit. Red at >= 90% of the limit:
               CPU is throttled, memory is about to be OOM-killed.
   [1mRDY / RST[0m   ready containers / all containers, and restarts.
   [1mDetail line[0m CPU and memory sparkline of the pod (last 40 session samples + now; memory
               coloured by % of its limit, pk = peak), node, pool, pod IP, QoS class, status
               and the last exit reason (OOMKilled ...).
   [1mTimeline[0m    namespace CPU and memory over the session (z window, c hides the graphs).

